    <div class="game_name">
        <div class="game_title">
            <h3>cricket</h3>
            <p>
                Cricket is a popular bat-and-ball sport played between two teams, each consisting of 11 players. It is
                particularly popular in countries like India, England, Australia, Pakistan, and South Africa. Here's a
                brief overview of cricket:

                <br> <b> Objective:</b> The primary objective of cricket is to score more runs than the opposing team
                while
                also
                dismissing their batsmen.

                <br> <b> Playing Field: </b>Cricket is played on an oval or circular field with a rectangular
                22-yard-long pitch at
                its center. The pitch is where most of the action takes place.

                <br> <b> Equipment: </b>Players use a wooden bat to hit a leather ball, and the fielding team tries to
                get the
                batsmen out using a variety of tactics. Protective gear like helmets, pads, and gloves are worn by
                batsmen and wicketkeepers for safety.

                <br> <b> Scoring:</b> Runs are scored by hitting the ball and running between two sets of stumps, called
                "wickets,"
                at either end of the pitch. Runs can also be scored by hitting boundaries, such as fours (ball crosses
                the boundary on the ground) and sixes (ball crosses the boundary in the air).

                <br> <b> Bowling and Fielding:</b> The bowling team aims to dismiss batsmen by getting them out in
                various ways, such
                as bowled (ball hits the stumps), caught (fielder catches the ball), lbw (leg before wicket), and more.
                Fielders support the bowlers by trying to prevent runs and take catches.

                <br> <b> Formats:</b> Cricket is played in different formats, including Test cricket (the longest format
                lasting up
                to five days), One Day Internationals (ODIs), and Twenty20 (T20) matches, which are shorter and
                faster-paced.

                <br> <b> International Competitions:</b> The most prestigious international cricket tournaments include
                the ICC
                Cricket World Cup for ODIs and the ICC World Twenty20 for T20 matches. National teams from various
                countries compete in these events.

                <br> <b> Domestic Leagues:</b> Many countries also have domestic cricket leagues, such as the Indian
                Premier League
                (IPL) and the Big Bash League (BBL), which feature top international and domestic players.

                <br> <b> Spirit of the Game:</b> Cricket is known for its strong emphasis on sportsmanship and fair
                play. It has a
                set of rules and a code of conduct that players are expected to follow.

                <br> <b> Cultural Significance:</b> Cricket is not just a sport; it often holds deep cultural and social
                significance
                in countries where it is popular, with matches attracting passionate fans and large audiences.

                Cricket is a sport that combines strategy, skill, and teamwork, and it has a rich history dating back
                centuries. It continues to evolve with new formats and innovations, making it a beloved sport for
                millions of fans around the world.
            </p>
        </div>

