    {{!-- sky diving--}}


    <div class="game_name game1">
        <div class="game_imgs">
            <img class="img1" src="images/skydiving_1.png" alt="">
            <h4>Gravity's marvel!</h4>

            <img src="images/skydiving_2.png" alt="">

        </div>

        <div class="game_title are1">
            <h3> skydiving</h3>
            <p>

                <br> <b> Skydiving</b> is an exhilarating adventure sport that involves jumping from an aircraft at high
                altitudes and
                free-falling before deploying a parachute to safely land on the ground. Here's some information about
                skydiving:

                <br> <b> Equipment:</b> Skydivers wear specialized gear that includes a jumpsuit, a parachute harness,
                an
                altimeter to
                measure altitude, and a parachute system. There are two main types of parachutes used in skydiving: the
                main
                parachute and the reserve parachute, which is a backup in case the main chute malfunctions.

                <br> <b>Training:</b> Before making a solo jump, individuals usually undergo training through a program
                like
                the
                Accelerated Freefall (AFF) or Static Line. These programs teach essential skills such as body
                positioning,
                altitude awareness, emergency procedures, and canopy control.

                <br> <b> Types of Skydiving:</b>

                <br> <b>Tandem Skydiving:</b> Beginners often start with a tandem jump, where they are harnessed to an
                experienced
                instructor who guides the jump.
                Solo Skydiving: After training, individuals can jump solo, either with a static line attached to the
                aircraft or by free-falling with an instructor nearby.
                Formation Skydiving: Experienced skydivers form groups and create formations during freefall, with
                synchronized movements and grips.
                Wingsuit Flying: Advanced skydivers can wear wingsuits that allow them to glide horizontally during
                freefall.
                <br> <b> BASE Jumping:</b> A more extreme form of skydiving involves jumping from fixed objects like
                cliffs,
                bridges, or
                buildings.
                Freefall: During freefall, which typically lasts for about a minute, skydivers experience the sensation
                of
                weightlessness and can reach speeds of up to 120 mph (193 km/h). It's an adrenaline-pumping experience.

                <br> <b> Canopy Flight:</b> After deploying the parachute, skydivers steer and control their descent
                using
                the canopy.
                They aim for a safe landing spot, usually a designated area on the ground.

                <br> <b>Safety: </b>Skydiving is generally safe when conducted with proper training and equipment.
                Instructors and
                jumpmasters play a crucial role in ensuring safety during jumps.

                <br> <b> Popular Drop Zones:</b> There are skydiving facilities, often referred to as drop zones,
                located
                around the
                world. Some renowned drop zones include Perris Valley Skydiving in California, Skydive Dubai in the UAE,
                and
                Interlaken in Switzerland.

                <br> <b> Records and Competitions:</b> Skydiving has various disciplines and competitions, including
                accuracy landing,
                canopy piloting, and artistic freefall. World records are regularly set in skydiving, such as the
                highest
                altitude jump and the largest formation.

                <br> <b> Community and Culture:</b> Skydiving has a tight-knit community of enthusiasts who share a
                passion for the sport. It often involves camaraderie and social gatherings at drop zones.

                Skydiving offers an unparalleled adrenaline rush and a sense of freedom that attracts thrill-seekers
                from
                around the world. Safety is paramount, and proper training is essential for anyone interested in
                experiencing the thrill of freefall.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

